{"name":"Flowery","hex":"#e4dcbf","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flowery","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to or characteristic of flowers.","Decorated with or abundant in flowers."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone or something considered flowery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flowery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flower (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Flower is a video game developed by Thatgamecompany and published by Sony Computer Entertainment for the PlayStation 3. It was designed by Jenova Chen and Nicholas Clark and was released in February 2009 on the PlayStation Network. PlayStation 4 and PlayStation Vita versions of the game were ported by Bluepoint Games and released in November 2013. An iOS version was released in September 2017, and a Windows version was released in February 2019, both published by Annapurna Interactive. The game was intended as a \"spiritual successor\" to Flow, a previous title by Chen and Thatgamecompany. In Flower, the player controls the wind, blowing a flower petal through the air using the movement of the game controller. Flying close to flowers results in the player's petal being followed by other flower petals. Approaching flowers may also have side-effects on the game world, such as bringing vibrant color to previously dead fields or activating stationary wind turbines. The game features no text or dialogue, forming a narrative arc primarily through visual representation and emotional cues."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ce/Flower_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q1825218"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ce/Flower_cover.png/250px-Flower_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/ce/Flower_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ce/Flower_cover.png/250px-Flower_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlower_cover.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f5/Flower_screen01.jpg/330px-Flower_screen01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f5/Flower_screen01.jpg/330px-Flower_screen01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A screenshot of Flower, showing a trail of flower petals as viewed by the player as they are blown through the air","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlower_screen01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Jenova_Chen_-_2007.jpg/500px-Jenova_Chen_-_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Jenova_Chen_-_2007.jpg/1280px-Jenova_Chen_-_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Jenova_Chen_-_2007.jpg/500px-Jenova_Chen_-_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Designer Jenova Chen in 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJenova_Chen_-_2007.jpg"}],"sounds":{"flowery":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-flowery.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/27/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-flowery.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-flowery.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"